{
 "sig": "8e9649cf5125",
 "text": "The Chinese had not only struck at Yudam-ni. They had struck everywhere at once. The road south to Hagaru-ri was cut. At Toktong Pass halfway down a single rifle company was surrounded on a lonely hill. At Hagaru-ri itself enemy troops stormed toward the half-finished airstrip. East of the reservoir the Army regiment known as Task Force Faith was fighting for its life.",
